# Tool risk policy (pn-core MCP)

| Tier | Tools | Expectation |
|------|-------|-------------|
| Read-only | `list_*`, `get_*`, `health`, `list_workflow_types`, `workflow_step`, `workflow_confirm`, `workflow_usage_totals`, `workflow_handoff_read`, `workflow_state_load` | No workspace writes; safe to call freely. |
| Append-only JSONL | `report_usage`, `gate_log_append`, `workflow_handoff_append`, `workflow_state_save` | Writes under cwd only via path rules; prefer `.pncore/` paths. Idempotent or append-only semantics. |
| Gate / secret | `approval_checkpoint` | Requires `PNCORE_APPROVAL_TOKEN` on server; optional `workflow_type` + `workflow_step` + `run_id` for human-gate tickets. |
| External side effects | `paperclip_issue_*` | Requires Paperclip env; treat as production API calls. |

## Workflow human gates

- Optional **mandatory** human gates: `PNCORE_REQUIRE_APPROVAL_FOR_WORKFLOWS` — each human `workflow_step` needs a fresh `approval_checkpoint` ticket.
- Echo **`run_id`** from `workflow_step` in state for every call; pass the same `run_id` to `approval_checkpoint` when issuing tickets so tickets bind to the run.

## Audit

- After gate outcomes, call **`gate_log_append`** with optional **`run_id`** for correlation with `.pncore/workflow-runs.jsonl`.
